    {
      "id": "math-expressions",
      "title": "Math Expressions",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "math-intro",
          "title": "Introduction to Math Nodes",
          "description": [
            "Math nodes allow you to perform mathematical calculations and define variables within your document.",
            "",
            "You can quickly create a math node by typing `@math()` or `$$` followed by a space at the beginning of a line.",
            "",
            "The math functionality is powered by mathjs, a powerful mathematics library that supports a wide range of operations.",
            "",
            "Results are calculated in real-time as you type and displayed below the expression.",
            "",
            "Tip: You can double-click on any mathematical result to instantly copy its value to your clipboard."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "basic-operations",
          "title": "Basic Arithmetic Operations",
          "description": [
            "You can perform standard arithmetic operations:",
            "",
            "- Addition: 2 + 3",
            "- Subtraction: 10 - 4",
            "- Multiplication: 6 * 7",
            "- Division: 15 / 3",
            "- Power: 2 ^ 3",
            "- Modulo: 17 % 5",
            "",
            "Complex expressions are also supported:",
            "- (5 + 3) * 2",
            "- 10 / (2 + 3)",
            "- 2 ^ (3 + 1)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "variables",
          "title": "Variable Assignment and Usage",
          "description": [
            "Define variables using the assignment syntax and use them in subsequent expressions:",
            "",
            "Syntax: variable_name = expression",
            "",
            "Examples:",
            "- x = 10",
            "- y = 5",
            "- z = x + y  (result: 15)",
            "- area = x * y  (result: 50)",
            "",
            "Variable naming rules:",
            "- Must start with a letter or underscore",
            "- Can contain letters, numbers, and underscores",
            "- Case-sensitive (x and X are different variables)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "advanced-functions",
          "title": "Advanced Mathematical Functions",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs provides many built-in functions:",
            "",
            "Trigonometric functions:",
            "- sin(0.5)",
            "- cos(1)",
            "- tan(0.25)",
            "",
            "Other functions:",
            "- sqrt(16)  (square root)",
            "- abs(-5)  (absolute value)",
            "- log(100)  (logarithm)",
            "- exp(2)  (exponential)",
            "- floor(3.7)  (round down)",
            "- ceil(3.2)  (round up)",
            "- round(3.5)  (round to nearest)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "constants",
          "title": "Mathematical Constants",
          "description": [
            "Use built-in mathematical constants:",
            "",
            "- pi  (π ≈ 3.14159)",
            "- e  (Euler's number ≈ 2.71828)",
            "- Infinity  (∞)",
            "- i  (imaginary unit)",
            "- phi  (golden ratio ≈ 1.61803)",
            "",
            "Examples:",
            "- 2 * pi",
            "- e ^ 2",
            "- sin(pi/2)",
            "- phi ^ 2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "symbolic-computation",
          "title": "Symbolic Computation (Advanced)",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports symbolic computation for algebraic operations:",
            "",
            "Simplify expressions:",
            "- simplify('3 + 2 / 4')  → '7 / 2'",
            "- simplify('2x + 3x')  → '5 * x'",
            "- simplify('x^2 + x + 3 + x^2')  → '2 * x ^ 2 + x + 3'",
            "",
            "Calculate derivatives:",
            "- derivative('x^2', 'x')  → '2 * x'",
            "- derivative('sin(2x)', 'x')  → '2 * cos(2 * x)'",
            "- derivative('2x^2 + 3x + 4', 'x')  → '4 * x + 3'",
            "",
            "Note: These advanced symbolic functions are available in mathjs but may require specific implementation in your current setup."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "matrix-operations",
          "title": "Matrix and Vector Operations",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports matrix and vector operations:",
            "",
            "Matrix creation:",
            "- matrix([1, 2, 3])",
            "- matrix([[1, 2], [3, 4]])",
            "",
            "Matrix operations:",
            "- matrix addition: A + B",
            "- matrix multiplication: A * B",
            "- matrix transpose: transpose(A)",
            "- matrix determinant: det(A)",
            "- matrix inverse: inv(A)",
            "",
            "Vector operations:",
            "- dot product: dot(a, b)",
            "- cross product: cross(a, b)",
            "- norm: norm(v)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "additional-functions",
          "title": "Additional Mathematical Functions",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs provides many more functions:",
            "",
            "Statistics:",
            "- mean([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- median([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- std([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- variance([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "",
            "Complex numbers:",
            "- complex(2, 3)",
            "- re(complex(2, 3))",
            "- im(complex(2, 3))",
            "",
            "Units:",
            "- unit('5 cm')",
            "- unit('2 kg').to('g')",
            "- unit('10 m/s') * unit('5 s')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "conversions",
          "title": "Unit Conversions",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports unit conversions for various measurement types:",
            "",
            "Angle conversions:",
            "- Degrees to radians: angle * pi/180",
            "- Radians to degrees: angle * 180/pi",
            "- Example: 90 * pi/180  (result: 1.5708 radians)",
            "",
            "Temperature conversions:",
            "- Celsius to Fahrenheit: (celsius * 9/5) + 32",
            "- Fahrenheit to Celsius: (fahrenheit - 32) * 5/9",
            "- Example: (25 * 9/5) + 32  (result: 77°F)",
            "",
            "Length conversions:",
            "- Meters to kilometers: meters / 1000",
            "- Kilometers to meters: kilometers * 1000",
            "- Meters to feet: meters * 3.28084",
            "- Example: 1000 / 1000  (result: 1 km)",
            "",
            "Weight conversions:",
            "- Kilograms to grams: kilograms * 1000",
            "- Grams to kilograms: grams / 1000",
            "- Kilograms to pounds: kilograms * 2.20462",
            "- Example: 5 * 2.20462  (result: 11.0231 lbs)",
            "",
            "Tips for conversions:",
            "- Use variables to store conversion factors",
            "- Chain conversions for complex unit changes",
            "- Document your conversion formulas with comments"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fractions",
          "title": "Fraction Calculations",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports exact fraction calculations to avoid floating-point precision issues:",
            "",
            "Creating fractions:",
            "- fraction(1, 3)  (creates 1/3)",
            "- fraction(3, 4)  (creates 3/4)",
            "- fraction(1, 2) + fraction(1, 3)  (result: 5/6)",
            "",
            "Fraction operations:",
            "- Addition: fraction(1, 4) + fraction(1, 4)  (result: 1/2)",
            "- Subtraction: fraction(3, 4) - fraction(1, 4)  (result: 1/2)",
            "- Multiplication: fraction(1, 2) * fraction(2, 3)  (result: 1/3)",
            "- Division: fraction(1, 2) / fraction(1, 4)  (result: 2)",
            "",
            "Converting to decimal:",
            "- fraction(1, 3).toNumber()  (result: 0.333...)",
            "- fraction(3, 4).toNumber()  (result: 0.75)",
            "",
            "Practical examples:",
            "- fraction(1, 3) + fraction(2, 3)  (result: 1)",
            "- fraction(2, 5) * 10  (result: 4)",
            "- fraction(7, 8) - fraction(1, 8)  (result: 3/4)",
            "",
            "Benefits of fractions:",
            "- Exact precision for rational numbers",
            "- Avoids floating-point rounding errors",
            "- Maintains mathematical exactness in calculations"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "formatting",
          "title": "Number Formatting",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs provides the format() function to display numbers in various formats:",
            "",
            "Basic formatting:",
            "- format(1234.5678, {notation: 'fixed'})  (result: '1234.567800')",
            "- format(1234.5678, {notation: 'fixed', precision: 2})  (result: '1234.57')",
            "- format(0.1234, {notation: 'exponential'})  (result: '1.234e-1')",
            "",
            "Available notations:",
            "- 'auto': Automatic notation selection",
            "- 'fixed': Fixed-point notation",
            "- 'exponential': Scientific notation",
            "- 'bin': Binary notation (with 0b prefix)",
            "- 'oct': Octal notation (with 0o prefix)",
            "- 'hex': Hexadecimal notation (with 0x prefix)",
            "",
            "Binary/octal/hex examples:",
            "- format(10, {notation: 'bin'})  (result: '0b1010')",
            "- format(10, {notation: 'oct'})  (result: '0o12')",
            "- format(255, {notation: 'hex'})  (result: '0xff')",
            "",
            "Precision control:",
            "- format(pi, {precision: 2})  (result: '3.1')",
            "- format(pi, {precision: 4})  (result: '3.1416')",
            "- format(123.456, {precision: 1})  (result: '123.5')",
            "",
            "Practical examples:",
            "- format(0.001234, {notation: 'exponential'})  (result: '1.234e-3')",
            "- format(1000, {notation: 'fixed', precision: 0})  (result: '1000')",
            "- format(16, {notation: 'hex'})  (result: '0x10')",
            "",
            "Benefits of formatting:",
            "- Present results in user-friendly formats",
            "- Choose appropriate notation for your use case",
            "- Control precision for display purposes",
            "- Convert between number systems (bin/oct/hex) with standard prefixes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "error-handling",
          "title": "Error Handling",
          "description": [
            "Math nodes provide visual feedback for errors:",
            "",
            "Common errors:",
            "- Division by zero: 5 / 0",
            "- Invalid syntax: 2 + * 3",
            "- Undefined variables: unknown_var + 5",
            "- Invalid values: sqrt(-1)",
            "",
            "Error display:",
            "- Errors appear in red at the bottom of the math node",
            "- Click on the error message to see full details",
            "- Results are automatically hidden when errors occur"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "math-examples",
          "title": "Practical Examples",
          "description": [
            "Example 1: Simple calculations",
            "price = 100",
            "tax = 0.2",
            "total = price * (1 + tax)  (result: 120)",
            "",
            "Example 2: Geometry calculations",
            "radius = 5",
            "area = pi * radius ^ 2  (result: 78.5398)",
            "circumference = 2 * pi * radius  (result: 31.4159)",
            "",
            "Example 3: Financial calculations",
            "principal = 1000",
            "rate = 0.05",
            "years = 3",
            "amount = principal * (1 + rate) ^ years  (result: 1157.625)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
