    {
      "id": "markdown-support",
      "title": "Markdown Support",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "markdown-intro",
          "title": "Markdown Shortcuts",
          "description": [
            "ANQL supports a wide range of Markdown shortcuts that allow you to format text and create complex blocks just by typing.",
            "Simply type the markdown syntax followed by a space to instantly transform the text."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "markdown-blocks",
          "title": "Block Elements",
          "description": [
            "Type these shortcuts at the beginning of a new line:",
            "",
            "- Headings: Type `# `, `## `, or `### ` for Headings 1, 2, and 3",
            "- Bullet List: Type `- `, `* `, or `+ `",
            "- Numbered List: Type `1. `",
            "- Check List: Type `- [ ] ` or `- [x] `",
            "- Blockquote: Type `> `",
            "- Code Block: Type ```` ```` followed by the language name (e.g., ```` ```javascript ````)",
            "- Horizontal Rule: Type `---`, `***`, or `___`",
            "- Math Block: Type `$$ ` or `@math() `",
            "- Table: Type `| column 1 | column 2 |` to start a table"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "markdown-inline",
          "title": "Inline Formatting",
          "description": [
            "Use these shortcuts anywhere in your text:",
            "",
            "- Bold: `**text**` or `__text__`",
            "- Italic: `*text*` or `_text_`",
            "- Strikethrough: `~~text~~`",
            "- Inline Code: ` `text` ` (wrap with single backticks)",
            "- Inline Math: `$equation$`",
            "- Links: `[Link text](https://example.com)`",
            "- Images: `![Alt text](image-url.jpg)`",
            "- Date: `@date(YYYY-MM-DD)`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
